# 12. Set vs Priority Queue

Since you just learned Priority Queue, don't mix these two.

| Feature        | Set                       | Priority Queue          |
| -------------- | ------------------------- | ----------------------- |
| Duplicates     | ❌                         | ✅                       |
| Main purpose   | Unique elements           | Highest/lowest priority |
| Sorted/ordered | Depends on implementation | Heap order              |
| Access         | Can iterate/search        | Mainly `top()`          |
| Remove         | Specific element possible | Removes top priority    |
| C++ example    | `set<int>`                | `priority_queue<int>`   |

Example:

### Set

```text
Input:  5 2 8 2 5

Set:
2 5 8
```

### Max Heap

```text
Input: 5 2 8 2 5

Priority Queue:
8 5 5 2 2
```

The priority queue **keeps duplicates**.

